#: css/rubric-note.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: rubric-note"
msgstr "# CSS: rubric-note"

#: css/rubric-note.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`div[class~=\"instui-rubric-note\"]` — Structured note with rubric categories and scoring indicators."
msgstr "`div[class~=\"instui-rubric-note\"]` — Note structurée avec catégories de rubrique et indicateurs de notation."

#: css/rubric-note.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "✅ Use Rubric-Note when:"
msgstr "✅ Utiliser Rubric-Note lorsque :"

#: css/rubric-note.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- Displaying grading rubric or assessment criteria\n- You need to structure content by category with scores or indicators\n- The layout should emphasize structure and hierarchy\n🚫 Don't use Rubric-Note when:"
msgstr "- Afficher une grille d'évaluation ou des critères d'évaluation\n- Vous devez structurer le contenu par catégorie avec des scores ou des indicateurs\n- La mise en page doit mettre l'accent sur la structure et la hiérarchie\n🚫 Ne pas utiliser Rubric-Note lorsque :"

#: css/rubric-note.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- Displaying simple notes or comments — use Callout instead\n- Complex grading logic is needed — consider a custom component"
msgstr "- Afficher des notes ou commentaires simples — utiliser Callout à la place\n- Une logique d'évaluation complexe est nécessaire — envisager un composant personnalisé"

#: css/rubric-note.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- Use table semantics if displaying a true rubric with rows and columns\n- Ensure score indicators are not color-only\n- Provide descriptive labels for each category"
msgstr "- Utiliser la sémantique de tableau si vous affichez une vraie grille avec lignes et colonnes\n- Veiller à ce que les indicateurs de score ne reposent pas uniquement sur la couleur\n- Fournir des libellés descriptifs pour chaque catégorie"

#: css/rubric-note.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Container for rubric criteria rows."
msgstr "Conteneur pour les lignes de critères de la rubrique."

#: css/rubric-note.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Detailed description of the criterion."
msgstr "Description détaillée du critère."

#: css/rubric-note.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Header with title and metadata."
msgstr "En-tête avec titre et métadonnées."

#: css/rubric-note.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Criterion name or category."
msgstr "Nom du critère ou catégorie."

#: css/rubric-note.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Individual criterion row."
msgstr "Ligne individuelle de critère."

#: css/rubric-note.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Score indicator or badge."
msgstr "Indicateur de score ou badge."

#: css/screen-reader-content.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: screen-reader-content"
msgstr "# CSS: screen-reader-content"

#: css/screen-reader-content.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-screen-reader-content` — Visually hides content while keeping it available to assistive tech (the standard clip pattern)."
msgstr "`.instui-screen-reader-content` — Masque visuellement le contenu tout en le laissant accessible aux technologies d'assistance (le motif standard de clip)."

#: css/screen-reader-content.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [screen-reader-content.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/utilities/screen-reader-content/screen-reader-content.css)"
msgstr "**Source:** [screen-reader-content.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/utilities/screen-reader-content/screen-reader-content.css)"

#: css/screen-reader-content.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Keeps text in the accessibility tree for screen readers while removing it from the visual layout."
msgstr "Conserve le texte dans l'arbre d'accessibilité pour les lecteurs d'écran tout en le retirant de la mise en page visuelle."

#: css/side-nav-bar.item.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: side-nav-bar.item"
msgstr "# CSS: side-nav-bar.item"

#: css/side-nav-bar.item.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.item` — A navigation entry (InstUI `SideNavBar.Item`); `-selected` marks the active one."
msgstr "`.item` — Une entrée de navigation (InstUI `SideNavBar.Item`); `-selected` indique celle qui est active."

#: css/side-nav-bar.item.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The parent `side-nav-bar`'s `-minimized` modifier hides this member's `.label` — see `side-nav-bar`'s own doc for that modifier."
msgstr "Le modificateur `-minimized` du parent `side-nav-bar` masque le `.label` de ce membre — voir la documentation de `side-nav-bar` pour ce modificateur."

#: css/side-nav-bar.item.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The active nav item."
msgstr "L'élément de navigation actif."

#: css/side-nav-bar.item.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The item's text label; hidden when the rail is minimized."
msgstr "L'étiquette textuelle de l'élément ; masquée lorsque le rail est réduit."

#: css/side-nav-bar.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: side-nav-bar"
msgstr "# CSS: side-nav-bar"

#: css/side-nav-bar.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-side-nav-bar` — A vertical navigation rail of icon-over-label items, with a minimized icons-only mode."
msgstr "`.instui-side-nav-bar` — Un rail de navigation vertical d'éléments icône-au-dessus-de-l'étiquette, avec un mode minimisé uniquement icônes."

#: css/side-nav-bar.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Sets its own `gap` between nav items and its own `padding`; chaining a `-gap-*`/`-p-*`/`-padding-*` spacing utility modifier overrides those built-in values. See the `side-nav-bar.item` member for the individual nav entries."
msgstr "Définit son propre `gap` entre les éléments de navigation et son propre `padding` ; le chaînage d'un modificateur utilitaire d'espacement `-gap-*`/`-p-*`/`-padding-*` remplace ces valeurs intégrées. Voir le membre `side-nav-bar.item` pour les entrées de navigation individuelles."

#: css/side-nav-bar.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [item.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/side-nav-bar/members/item/item.css)"
msgstr "**Source:** [item.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/side-nav-bar/members/item/item.css)"

#: css/side-nav-bar.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Label the `<nav>` with aria-label so it's announced as a named navigation landmark."
msgstr "Label the `&lt;nav&gt;` with aria-label so it's announced as a named navigation landmark."

#: css/side-nav-bar.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Render a glyph icon in each nav item."
msgstr "Afficher une icône glyphe dans chaque élément de navigation."

#: css/side-nav-bar.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Collapse to icons only (labels hidden). @affects side-nav-bar.item — Hides the item's label."
msgstr "Réduire aux seules icônes (étiquettes masquées). @affects side-nav-bar.item — Masque l'étiquette de l'élément."

#: css/side-nav-bar.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The nav item's text label."
msgstr "Le libellé textuel de l'élément de navigation."

#: css/simple-select.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: simple-select"
msgstr "# CSS: simple-select"

#: css/simple-select.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-simple-select` — A styled native `<select>` with a caret, matching the text-input states and sizes."
msgstr "`.instui-simple-select` — A styled native `&lt;select&gt;` with a caret, matching the text-input states and sizes."

#: css/simple-select.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Wraps a plain native `<select>` with no custom dropdown/menu markup, so browser-native option rendering and keyboard behavior apply as-is; it shares its field chrome with `text-input`."
msgstr "Wraps a plain native `&lt;select&gt;` with no custom dropdown/menu markup, so browser-native option rendering and keyboard behavior apply as-is; it shares its field chrome with `text-input`."

#: css/simple-select.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [select.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/select/select.css)"
msgstr "**Source :** [select.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/select/select.css)"

#: css/simple-select.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The placeholder text, in a muted color that shifts on hover."
msgstr "Le texte d'espace réservé, dans une couleur atténuée qui change au survol."

#: css/simple-select.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [text-input](/api/css/text-input.md) — Shares the same field chrome, states, and sizes.\n- [menu](/api/css/menu.md) — The dropdown surface a richer select reuses."
msgstr "- [text-input](/fr/api/css/text-input.md) — Shares the same field chrome, states, and sizes.\n- [menu](/fr/api/css/menu.md) — The dropdown surface a richer select reuses."

#: css/spacing.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: spacing"
msgstr "# CSS: spacing"

#: css/spacing.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.--p-md` — Margin and padding utilities — `.--m<side>-<step>` / `.--margin-<side>-<step>` and `.--p<side>-<step>` / `.--padding-<side>-<step>` on the spacing scale (sides `t`/`b`/`s`/`e`/`x`/`y` or none, spelled short or fully long — for example `--mb-sm` and `--margin-bottom-small` are the same rule; margin also takes `auto`). Usable bare or chained onto any component (for example `class=\"instui-view --mb-sm\"`)."
msgstr "`.--p-md` — Margin and padding utilities — `.--m&lt;side&gt;-&lt;step&gt;` / `.--margin-&lt;side&gt;-&lt;step&gt;` and `.--p&lt;side&gt;-&lt;step&gt;` / `.--padding-&lt;side&gt;-&lt;step&gt;` on the spacing scale (sides `t`/`b`/`s`/`e`/`x`/`y` or none, spelled short or fully long — for example `--mb-sm` and `--margin-bottom-small` are the same rule; margin also takes `auto`). Usable bare or chained onto any component (for example `class=\"instui-view --mb-sm\"`)."

#: css/spacing.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [index.ts](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/utilities/spacing/index.ts)"
msgstr "**Source :** [index.ts](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/utilities/spacing/index.ts)"

#: css/spacing.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Applies medium padding on all sides."
msgstr "Applique un padding moyen sur tous les côtés."

#: css/spacing.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Margin utilities across short, legacy-long, and fully long spellings."
msgstr "Utilitaires de marge pour les variantes short, legacy-long et fully long."

#: css/spacing.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Padding utilities across short, legacy-long, and fully long spellings."
msgstr "Utilitaires de padding pour les variantes short, legacy-long et fully long."

#: css/spinner.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: spinner"
msgstr "# CSS: spinner"

#: css/spinner.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-spinner` — An animated loading ring; give it role=\"status\" and an aria-label."
msgstr "`.instui-spinner` — Un anneau de chargement animé ; donnez-lui role=\"status\" et un aria-label."

#: css/spinner.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`-color-inverse` only repaints the animated top border segment, not the whole track, so it still reads correctly on a dark card without needing a separate track color."
msgstr "`-color-inverse` ne repeint que le segment de bord supérieur animé, pas toute la piste, donc il reste lisible sur une carte sombre sans nécessiter une couleur de piste séparée."

#: css/spinner.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [spinner.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/spinner/spinner.css)"
msgstr "**Source :** [spinner.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/spinner/spinner.css)"

#: css/spinner.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Give the spinner role=\"status\" and an aria-label so screen readers announce it as a live loading status."
msgstr "Donnez au spinner role=\"status\" et un aria-label afin que les lecteurs d'écran l'annoncent comme un état de chargement en direct."

#: css/spinner.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "### Inverse color -nocard"
