#: css/table.body.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: table.body"
msgstr "# CSS: table.body"

#: css/table.body.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`tbody` — The table's data row group (InstUI `Table.Body`)."
msgstr "`tbody` — Le groupe de lignes de données du tableau (InstUI `Table.Body`)."

#: css/table.body.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The parent `table`'s `-layout-stacked` modifier restyles this member — see `table`'s own doc for that modifier."
msgstr "Le modificateur `-layout-stacked` du parent `table` modifie le style de ce membre — voir la documentation propre de `table` pour ce modificateur."

#: css/table.cell.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: table.cell"
msgstr "# CSS: table.cell"

#: css/table.cell.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`td` — A data cell (InstUI `Table.Cell`)."
msgstr "`td` — Une cellule de données (InstUI `Table.Cell`)."

#: css/table.cell.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The parent `table`'s `-layout-stacked` modifier stacks this member as a block and labels it via `::before` — see `table`'s own doc for that modifier."
msgstr "Le modificateur `-layout-stacked` du parent `table` positionne ce membre comme un bloc et l'étiquette via `::before` — voir la documentation de `table` pour ce modificateur."

#: css/table.col-header.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: table.col-header"
msgstr "# CSS: table.col-header"

#: css/table.col-header.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`th` — A column-header cell (InstUI `Table.ColHeader`); the default `th` styling, overridden by `table.row-header` for `th[scope=\"row\"]`."
msgstr "`th` — Une cellule d'en-tête de colonne (InstUI `Table.ColHeader`) ; le style `th` par défaut, remplacé par `table.row-header` pour `th[scope=\"row\"]`."

#: css/table.head.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: table.head"
msgstr "# CSS: table.head"

#: css/table.head.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`thead` — The table's header row group (InstUI `Table.Head`)."
msgstr "`thead` — Le groupe de lignes d'en-tête du tableau (InstUI `Table.Head`)."

#: css/table.head.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The parent `table`'s `-layout-stacked` modifier visually hides this member (its column titles surface per-cell instead) — see `table`'s own doc for that modifier."
msgstr "Le modificateur `-layout-stacked` du parent `table` masque visuellement cet élément (les titres de colonne apparaissent par cellule à la place) — voir la documentation de `table` pour ce modificateur."

#: css/table.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: table"
msgstr "# CSS: table"

#: css/table.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-table` — A styled data table for `th` and `td` plus an optional caption, with hover, fixed, and stacked-card layouts."
msgstr "`.instui-table` — Un tableau de données stylisé pour `th` et `td` avec une légende optionnelle, proposant des dispositions au survol, fixe et en cartes empilées."

#: css/table.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "For `-layout-stacked`, pure CSS can't pull each column header's text into its cell, so give every cell a `data-label` and the stacked card shows it via `::before`. See the `table.head`, `table.body`, `table.row`, `table.cell`, `table.col-header`, and `table.row-header` members for the individual parts."
msgstr "Pour `-layout-stacked`, le CSS pur ne peut pas injecter le texte de chaque en-tête de colonne dans sa cellule ; donnez donc à chaque cellule un `data-label` et la carte empilée l'affiche via `::before`. Voir les membres `table.head`, `table.body`, `table.row`, `table.cell`, `table.col-header` et `table.row-header` pour les parties individuelles."

#: css/table.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [body.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/table/members/body/body.css)"
msgstr "**Source :** [body.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/table/members/body/body.css)"

#: css/table.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Label the table with a `<caption>`, mark column headers `<th scope=\"col\">` and row headers `<th scope=\"row\">`, and in `-layout-stacked` give every cell a `data-label` since the header row is visually hidden."
msgstr "Label the table with a `&lt;caption&gt;`, mark column headers `<th scope=\"col\">` and row headers `<th scope=\"row\">`, and in `-layout-stacked` give every cell a `data-label` since the header row is visually hidden."

#: css/table.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Highlight rows on hover. @affects table.row — Reserves and colours the row's hover border."
msgstr "Met en surbrillance les lignes au survol. @affects table.row — Réserve et colore la bordure de survol de la ligne."

#: css/table.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Fixed table layout (equal-width columns)."
msgstr "Disposition de table fixe (colonnes de largeur égale)."

#: css/table.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Stack each row as a card, via a per-cell `data-label`. @affects table.head @affects table.body @affects table.row @affects table.cell @affects table.col-header @affects table.row-header — Stacks each part as a block and hides/labels the header accordingly."
msgstr "Empile chaque ligne comme une carte, via un `data-label` par cellule. @affects table.head @affects table.body @affects table.row @affects table.cell @affects table.col-header @affects table.row-header — Empile chaque partie en tant que bloc et masque/étiquette l'en-tête en conséquence."

#: css/table.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "An optional table caption."
msgstr "Une légende de tableau optionnelle."

#: css/table.row-header.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: table.row-header"
msgstr "# CSS: table.row-header"

#: css/table.row-header.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`th[scope=\"row\"]` — A row-header cell (InstUI `Table.RowHeader`); styled from the row-header tokens, not the column-header ones."
msgstr "`th[scope=\"row\"]` — Une cellule d'en-tête de ligne (InstUI `Table.RowHeader`); stylisée à partir des tokens d'en-tête de ligne, pas de ceux d'en-tête de colonne."

#: css/table.row.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: table.row"
msgstr "# CSS: table.row"

#: css/table.row.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`tr` — A table row (InstUI `Table.Row`)."
msgstr "`tr` — Une ligne de tableau (InstUI `Table.Row`)."

#: css/table.row.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The parent `table`'s `-hover` and `-layout-stacked` modifiers restyle this member — see `table`'s own doc for those modifiers."
msgstr "Les modificateurs `-hover` et `-layout-stacked` du parent `table` restylent cet élément — voir la documentation de `table` pour ces modificateurs."

#: css/tabs.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: tabs"
msgstr "# CSS: tabs"

#: css/tabs.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-tabs` — A tabbed panel set: a tab list, selectable tabs, and their panels."
msgstr "`.instui-tabs` — Un ensemble d'onglets avec panneaux : une liste d'onglets, des onglets sélectionnables et leurs panneaux."

#: css/tabs.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "See the `tabs.tab` and `tabs.panel` members for the individual tab buttons and their content panels."
msgstr "Voir les membres `tabs.tab` et `tabs.panel` pour les boutons d'onglet individuels et leurs panneaux de contenu."

#: css/tabs.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [panel.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/tabs/members/panel/panel.css)"
msgstr "**Source :** [panel.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/tabs/members/panel/panel.css)"

#: css/tabs.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Wire the tab list with role=\"tablist\", each tab with role=\"tab\" and aria-selected, and each panel with role=\"tabpanel\"."
msgstr "Relier la liste d'onglets avec role=\"tablist\", chaque onglet avec role=\"tab\" et aria-selected, et chaque panneau avec role=\"tabpanel\"."

#: css/tabs.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Keep the tab list on one line and let it scroll horizontally instead of wrapping, hiding the scrollbar."
msgstr "Garder la liste d'onglets sur une seule ligne et la faire défiler horizontalement plutôt que de la renvoyer à la ligne, en masquant la barre de défilement."

#: css/tabs.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Rounded \"folder\" tabs with a selected tab that visually connects into the panel below. @affects tabs.tab — Restyles the tab buttons into the rounded \"folder\" look."
msgstr "Onglets « dossier » arrondis avec un onglet sélectionné qui se raccorde visuellement au panneau ci‑dessous. @affects tabs.tab — Redessine les boutons d'onglet pour leur donner l'apparence arrondie « dossier ». "

#: css/tabs.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The row of tabs."
msgstr "La rangée d'onglets."

#: css/tabs.panel.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: tabs.panel"
msgstr "# CSS: tabs.panel"

#: css/tabs.panel.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.panel` — The content panel for a tab (InstUI `Tabs.Panel`)."
msgstr "`.panel` — Le panneau de contenu d'un onglet (InstUI `Tabs.Panel`)."

#: css/tabs.tab.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: tabs.tab"
msgstr "# CSS: tabs.tab"

#: css/tabs.tab.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.tab` — A single tab button (InstUI `Tabs.Tab`, configured via the parent `Tabs`'s tab list); `-selected` marks the active one."
msgstr "`.tab` — Un seul bouton d'onglet (InstUI `Tabs.Tab`, configuré via la liste d'onglets du parent `Tabs`); `-selected` marque celui actif."

#: css/tabs.tab.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The parent `tabs`'s `-variant-secondary` modifier restyles this member into a rounded \"folder\" tab — see `tabs`'s own doc for that modifier."
msgstr "Le modificateur `-variant-secondary` du parent `tabs` transforme ce membre en onglet « dossier » arrondi — voir la propre documentation de `tabs` pour ce modificateur."

#: css/tabs.tab.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Non-interactive; same styling as `[aria-disabled=\"true\"]`/`:disabled`."
msgstr "Non interactif; même style que `[aria-disabled=\"true\"]`/`:disabled`."

#: css/tabs.tab.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The active tab; same styling as `[aria-selected=\"true\"]`."
msgstr "L'onglet actif; même style que `[aria-selected=\"true\"]`."

#: css/tag.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: tag"
msgstr "# CSS: tag"

#: css/tag.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-tag` — An inline chip for a keyword or filter."
msgstr "`.instui-tag` — Une puce en ligne pour un mot-clé ou un filtre."

#: css/tag.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Sets its own horizontal `padding` (`-size-sm`/`-size-lg` scale it); chaining a `-p-*`/`-padding-*` spacing utility modifier overrides that built-in value."
msgstr "Définit sa propre `padding` horizontale (les `-size-sm`/`-size-lg` la redimensionnent) ; enchaîner un modificateur utilitaire d'espacement `-p-*`/`-padding-*` remplace cette valeur intégrée."

#: css/tag.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [tag.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/tag/tag.css)"
msgstr "**Source:** [tag.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/tag/tag.css)"

#: css/tag.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Reads inline with text and gets a trailing dismiss glyph."
msgstr "Se lit en ligne avec le texte et reçoit un glyphe de fermeture en fin."

#: css/tag.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Read-only (non-dismissable) tag."
msgstr "Étiquette en lecture seule (non supprimable)."

#: css/tag.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A large tag. Long-form alias of `-size-lg`."
msgstr "Une grande étiquette. Alias en forme longue de `-size-lg`."

#: css/tag.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A large tag."
msgstr "Une grande étiquette."

#: css/tag.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A small tag."
msgstr "Une petite étiquette."

#: css/tag.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A small tag. Long-form alias of `-size-sm`."
msgstr "Une petite étiquette. Alias en forme longue de `-size-sm`."

#: css/tag.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Renders the trailing dismiss glyph on a dismissible inline tag."
msgstr "Affiche le glyphe de fermeture final sur une étiquette en ligne supprimable."

#: css/tag.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [pill](/api/css/pill.md) — The read-only label-chip counterpart."
msgstr "- [pill](/fr/api/css/pill.md) — The read-only label-chip counterpart."

#: css/testimonial.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: testimonial"
msgstr "# CSS: testimonial"

#: css/testimonial.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`div[class~=\"instui-testimonial\"]` — Quote or testimonial display with attribution and optional imagery."
msgstr "`div[class~=\"instui-testimonial\"]` — Affichage de citation ou témoignage avec attribution et images facultatives."

#: css/testimonial.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "✅ Use Testimonial when:"
msgstr "✅ Utiliser Testimonial lorsque :"

#: css/testimonial.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- Displaying customer or user testimonials and quotes\n- You want to highlight a statement with visual emphasis\n- Attribution and context (name, title, image) are important\n🚫 Don't use Testimonial when:"
msgstr "- Afficher des témoignages et citations de clients ou d'utilisateurs\n- Vous voulez mettre en valeur une déclaration avec une emphase visuelle\n- L'attribution et le contexte (nom, titre, image) sont importants\n🚫 Ne pas utiliser Testimonial lorsque :"

#: css/testimonial.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- Displaying inline quotes in body text — use a blockquote element instead\n- The statement is the main focus — use Hero or Card instead"
msgstr "- Afficher des citations en ligne dans le texte — utilisez plutôt un élément blockquote\n- La déclaration est le point principal — utilisez plutôt Hero ou Card"

#: css/testimonial.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- Use `<blockquote>` semantically for the quote\n- Ensure attribution is clear and associated with the quote\n- If using images, provide alt text"
msgstr "- Use `&lt;blockquote&gt;` semantically for the quote\n- Ensure attribution is clear and associated with the quote\n- If using images, provide alt text"

#: css/testimonial.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Attribution author name."
msgstr "Nom de l'auteur pour l'attribution."

#: css/testimonial.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Optional author profile image."
msgstr "Image de profil de l'auteur (facultative)."

#: css/testimonial.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Container for quote and attribution."
msgstr "Conteneur pour la citation et l'attribution."

#: css/testimonial.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The quoted text."
msgstr "Le texte cité."

#: css/testimonial.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Optional author title or affiliation."
msgstr "Titre ou affiliation de l'auteur (facultatif)."

#: css/text-area.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: text-area"
msgstr "# CSS: text-area"

#: css/text-area.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-text-area` — A styled, resizable native `<textarea>` with the same states and sizes as the text input."
msgstr "`.instui-text-area` — A styled, resizable native `&lt;textarea&gt;` with the same states and sizes as the text input."

#: css/text-area.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Shares its border, background, and focus states with `text-input` and `simple-select`; only `resize: vertical` and the taller minimum height are unique to it."
msgstr "Partage ses états de bordure, d'arrière-plan et de focus avec `text-input` et `simple-select` ; seuls `resize: vertical` et la hauteur minimale plus élevée lui sont propres."

#: css/text-area.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [text-area.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/text-area/text-area.css)"
msgstr "**Source :** [text-area.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/text-area/text-area.css)"

#: css/text-area.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [text-input](/api/css/text-input.md) — The single-line counterpart with the same states and sizes."
msgstr "- [text-input](/fr/api/css/text-input.md) — The single-line counterpart with the same states and sizes."

#: css/text-input.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: text-input"
msgstr "# CSS: text-input"

#: css/text-input.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-text-input` — A styled native `<input>` — including `date`, `time`, and `datetime-local`, where the browser supplies the picker — with validation states and sizes."
msgstr "`.instui-text-input` — A styled native `&lt;input&gt;` — including `date`, `time`, and `datetime-local`, where the browser supplies the picker — with validation states and sizes."

#: css/text-input.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Shares its border, background, and state chrome with `text-area`, `simple-select`, `number-input`, and `input-group`; for `date`/`time`/`datetime-local` types the browser supplies its own picker UI, which this stylesheet doesn't style."
msgstr "Partage sa bordure, son arrière-plan et le chrome d'état avec `text-area`, `simple-select`, `number-input` et `input-group` ; pour les types `date`/`time`/`datetime-local`, le navigateur fournit sa propre interface de sélection, que cette feuille de style ne stylise pas."

#: css/text-input.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [text-input.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/text-input/text-input.css)"
msgstr "**Source :** [text-input.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/text-input/text-input.css)"

#: css/text-input.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [text-area](/api/css/text-area.md) — The multi-line counterpart with the same states and sizes.\n- [number-input](/api/css/number-input.md) — The numeric-entry input sharing this chrome.\n- [simple-select](/api/css/simple-select.md) — The native select sharing this field chrome.\n- [input-group](/api/css/input-group.md) — Wraps this input with leading and trailing slots."
msgstr "- [text-area](/fr/api/css/text-area.md) — The multi-line counterpart with the same states and sizes.\n- [number-input](/fr/api/css/number-input.md) — The numeric-entry input sharing this chrome.\n- [simple-select](/fr/api/css/simple-select.md) — The native select sharing this field chrome.\n- [input-group](/fr/api/css/input-group.md) — Wraps this input with leading and trailing slots."

#: css/text.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: text"
msgstr "# CSS: text"

#: css/text.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-text` · <span class=\"instui-pill -color-success pantoken-doc-tag\">stable</span> — Body-text typography with size, weight, colour, and style modifiers."
msgstr "`.instui-text` · <span class=\"instui-pill -color-success pantoken-doc-tag\">stable</span> — Typographie du texte de corps avec modificateurs de taille, poids, couleur et style."

#: css/text.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The `-variant-*` presets and the `-color-*`/`-size-*`/`-weight-*` modifiers all compose on the same element; unlike `heading`, it renders no implicit semantic level."
msgstr "Les presets `-variant-*` et les modificateurs `-color-*`/`-size-*`/`-weight-*` se composent tous sur le même élément ; contrairement à `heading`, il n'implique aucun niveau sémantique implicite."

